  "decomposition_method": "likelihood_breakdown.call_accounting wraps ~40 named library descriptors and three module-level solver functions and the PRODUCTION AnalysisImaging.log_likelihood_function is then run untouched. Each row is inclusive time, exclusive (self) time and the number of times the library reached the site; exclusive times are additive by construction, so 'unattributed' is a measured remainder and not an estimate. It is always an explicit row. Rows are rescaled by decomposition_rescale_factor (clean / instrumented) so they sum to the quoted, uninstrumented call. The clean and instrumented calls are COUNTERBALANCED (A B B A per block), so the overhead ratio is free of any drift linear in call index, and the warm-up runs to a steady state with its whole per-call sequence recorded under rows[*].warmup.",
